    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Most of us rush, but flossing rewards patience. One careful night saves days of sore gums later."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Maintaining Oral Hygiene During Orthodontic Treatment"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "While you wear braces, your mouth needs extra care. The combination of brushing and flossing keeps your oral hygiene balanced. Floss threaders are small but mighty, they reach where nothing else can."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Pair them with water flossers once a week to clean around tight spaces and the arch wire. Add fluoride toothpaste to keep tooth enamel strong. Avoid sugary snacks between meals, sugar hides under the wire longer than you think."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A clean mouth also keeps adjustments smooth. Orthodontists can work faster when they see less buildup. That’s one hidden perk of good oral hygiene."
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Final Thoughts"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Learning to floss with braces isn’t just about clean teeth. It’s about patience, routine, and care. The time you spend now protects your gums, prevents tooth decay, and keeps your smile healthy for life."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "If you’re struggling with technique or need a demo, visit Dr Dante Gonzales Orthodontics. We can show you the right way to use a floss threader, recommend suitable flossing tools, and help you build a practical oral hygiene routine that fits your schedule."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Keep it simple, brush and floss, stay consistent, and your beautiful smile will thank you later."
    },
