    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. How often should I floss with braces? Floss once daily or at least every alternate day. It helps remove plaque and prevents gum inflammation during your braces journey. 2. What’s the best floss to use with braces? Waxed floss or dental tape works best. They slide easily around brackets and wires without tearing. 3. Are floss threaders necessary? Yes, a floss threader makes flossing with braces faster. It helps guide the string floss under the arch wire safely. 4. Can water flossers replace traditional flossing? Water flossers are great for sensitive gums and quick cleaning, but pair them with traditional flossing for complete removal of plaque and debris. 5. What happens if I skip flossing during orthodontic treatment? Skipping flossing leads to plaque, tooth decay, and gum disease. Stick to your oral hygiene routine to keep your smile shining and gums healthy."
